{"questions":[{"id":"kirk-17476a9c55b97386-q31","question_number":"2","source":{"course":"Physics","level":"SL","year":1998,"session":"Guide reproduction","collection":"supplementary","collection_label":"Tim Kirk · Oxford 2003 · 1998 question reproductions","paper_label":"3","syllabus":"legacy"},"parts":[{"label":"whole","marks":null,"review_status":"reviewed","subtopic_ids":["A.4"],"depends_on":[],"context_ids":[],"assets":[{"path":"practice/supplement/kirk-17476a9c55b97386-written-31-46e772dde99517ac.webp","pdf_page":114,"crop_pdf_points_top_left":[59,287,249,262],"dpi":144,"source_sha256":"17476a9c55b97386b5914e46d41435e1e1c02ca7a91476ee72e38a6c46f399d6"}],"answer":{"text":"A reasonable centre of mass is about 20 cm from the elbow, shifted toward the hand relative to a uniform forearm because the hand adds mass. Torque from the weight ≈ 1.7 × 9.8 × 0.20 = 3.3 N m (about 3.4 N m). With a 5.0 cm muscle moment arm, the balancing tension is approximately 3.4/0.050 = 68 N.","source_id":"kirk-17476a9c55b97386","status":"editorial-solution","assets":[],"source":{"id":"kirk-17476a9c55b97386","path":"supplementary/pre-1999-questions/Physics_Study_Guide_Tim_Kirk_Oxford_2003.pdf","sha256":"17476a9c55b97386b5914e46d41435e1e1c02ca7a91476ee72e38a6c46f399d6","url":"https://ibdocs.re/p/IB%20BOOKS/Group%204%20-%20Sciences/Physics/OXFORD/Physics%20-%20Study%20Guide%20-%20Tim%20Kirk%20-%20First%20Edition%20-%20Oxford%202003.pdf","course":"Physics","level":"Mixed levels","year":1998,"session":"Guide reproduction","timezone":"","syllabus":"legacy","paper_label":"Mixed","material_type":"Historical guide reproduction","collection":"supplementary","collection_label":"Tim Kirk · Oxford 2003 · 1998 question reproductions","title":"1998 IB Physics questions reproduced in Tim Kirk's study guide"}}}],"contexts":[]},{"id":"sup-064316255265a882-0SL3w6","question_number":"6","source":{"course":"Physics","level":"SL","year":2016,"session":"Specimen","collection":"supplementary","collection_label